WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.220
Speaker 1: Mitt Romney was asked now that&nbsp;
George Anthony divulged there. Santos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.820
has been charged criminally with&nbsp;
multiple charges. What should happen?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:16.140
And I love that Mitt Romney doesn't just say he&nbsp;
should resign. He says he should already have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:23.040
resigned. And this is exactly the right answer.&nbsp;
I actually wish that there were more Republicans.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.660
Some of them are going to come around now and&nbsp;
say, well, he should now resign. I wish more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.860
people said what Mitt Romney says in this&nbsp;
short six second clip to CNN's Manu Raju.&nbsp;

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:36.420
Speaker 4: He should have resigned a long&nbsp;
time ago. He's an embarrassment to our party.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:42.300
He's an embarrassment to United States Congress.
Speaker 1: Okay. So, yes, he should resign now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:47.160
And actually, Republicans in the House should&nbsp;
hold a vote and they should kick him out. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:52.380
the right take, as Mitt Romney has been, one of&nbsp;
the few Republican voices willing to say this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:58.680
is that he should have been gone a long time ago.&nbsp;
He never should have gotten to this point in time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:06.840
even in even prior to the actual indictments.&nbsp;
These Republicans seem very scared to just come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.680
out and say it or they don't believe it, But&nbsp;
good for Mitt Romney for making that clear.

